id: pm-csv-sdk-write-fence
title: Adopt native SDK persistence fencing for CSV edits and compensation
description: "Audit G2 adoption, companion pm-cli-website-sumw. Upstream #1549 is closed and its SDK lease/persistence APIs are available. Remove callback deadline workarounds, use native mutateItem fencing and acquireLockLease().fence() for snapshots, settings and raw representation/history boundaries. Preserve CSV history-prefix conflict detection, original representation recovery and resumable compensation. Supported and tested SDK floor: 2026.11.5."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1549"
created_at: "2026-10-22T13:46:22.966Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T12:34:23.303Z"
author: codex-agent
expected_result: "The host atomically refuses stale item persistence when lease ownership or document revision changed, preserving the newer value and allowing safe transaction reconciliation."
actual_result: "The supported SDK floor is 2026.11.5. Native mutateItem fences callback and host-hook persistence; explicit LockLease.fence protects snapshots, settings and representation plus append-only completion history. The package deadline helper is removed. Separate-process expiry/takeover tests preserve newer bytes and history; exact-function reverts expose the old deadline refusals and unfenced representation window. Upstream #1549 is fixed; no unavailable fence is claimed."
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T16:12:05.186Z",codex-agent,"Owner-authorized callback deadline mitigation is implemented and covered in the normal suite. pm test pm-csv-sdk-write-fence --run --progress --timeout 600 passed 2/2 real takeover regressions, preserving newer SDK and separate CLI values with typed csv_lease_expired. Restoring only guardEditMutation fails both cases (0/2, exit 1, newer values overwritten), then restored fixed bytes pass. Both full npm and Bun release gates pass 315/315 and unchanged 100/100/100 coverage across six sources. Atomic persistence fencing still belongs upstream in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1549; arbitrary SDK delays outside the callback remain unprotected. Retain this item in progress for orchestrator/upstream verification and release the claim."
  "2026-10-23T11:12:27.825Z",codex-agent,"PR 177 compatibility assessment: pm-cli 2026.10.23 release and PR 1550 implement GH-1549 native lease/revision fencing. Real unguarded SDK takeover probe loses the newer title on 2026.10.20 but refuses stale persistence and preserves the newer title on 2026.10.23. A future supported-host-floor upgrade can replace callback-only csv_lease_expired guards on native paths with host lock_lost/stale_revision refusal coverage; extension lock overrides remain provider-owned. No pins or mitigation changed in this PR. Evidence: docs/compatibility-2026.10.20.md."
  "2026-10-23T15:31:43.780Z",codex-agent,"STALE-CLAIM: audited main cca10876ae5a4fcb505ffe533e00211941659ecc; no open PR or recently pushed live branch references this record. Inspected: docs/compatibility-2026.10.20.md, lease-guard.ts. Remaining: Upstream 2026.10.23 fencing is recorded, but this repo retains the older supported host and callback mitigation. Supported-floor migration and native lock_lost/stale_revision coverage remain; an upstream fix alone is not delivery here. Release historical contention and retain real work as open; no delivery/cancellation is claimed."
  "2026-11-06T12:10:36.244Z",codex-sol,"Implementing audit G2 from companion pm-cli-website-sumw (read only). Upstream #1549 is closed; replace deadline mitigation with public SDK lease/persistence fencing, audit representation recovery separately, retain history-prefix and foreign-writer guards. Raise the supported SDK floor as required by adoption. Same PR fixes gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214 through pm-csv-lewj. Real non-git trackers, separate-process takeover and behavioral reverts will verify the change."
  "2026-11-06T12:21:01.691Z",codex-sol,"Public SDK inspection: acquireLockLease returns LockLease.fence and native mutateItem fences the persistence boundary after callback and beforeMutation hooks. mutateItem has no raw-representation option; the second representation phase retains exact empty values under one public fence spanning writeFileAtomic plus appendHistoryEntry. It remains resumable across process interruption rather than a multi-file crash-atomic commit. No missing upstream fence is claimed. Package, manifest and development SDK now declare 2026.11.5."
  "2026-11-06T12:34:00.798Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral reverts in a disposable copy: restoring the exact original snapshot, captureUpdateCompensation and applyPlan functions each fails its slow-owner regression (0/1); restoring compensateUpdate fails the separate-process representation/history exclusion test (0/1). Removing only the representation fence also fails (0/1). Native callbacks and post-callback host delay preserve newer item bytes and history on real tracker takeover. Mutation-intent/settings targeted suite passes 15/15; focused append-only history guard passes 1/1 after fixing await-before-release in snapshot capture. Full release gates and current-head bot review remain PR gates."
  "2026-11-06T12:34:18.811Z",codex-sol,"Linked PM verification passes: original SDK/CLI takeover command 2/2 and lease/fencing suite 13/13, zero failures/skips. Linked admission suite passes 6/6. The inherited linked command required explicit clone-local trust acknowledgement because its historical source ref differs; after reviewing the exact command, both linked commands executed successfully. Automatic result persistence is disabled by existing tracker policy, so this comment records the receipts without changing policy. npm lint, typecheck, test typecheck, docstrings and duplication checks pass. Claims are released for orchestrator verification; items remain in_progress until reviewed."
